resses (receipt server, pass server, gift claim page, model address, logo), PINs and badge hashes, staff names, the ABN, address, phone and email on receipts are reported as *set* or left out. Counts of owners, managers and cashiers are given, not names (staff names are customer details, Revision 19). The Shopify store's own domain is included when connected. **(4) The reader's ready state counts as the app's own state, not as a terminal detail.** The rules table in 3.1 never sends terminal details, but 3.2 tool 15 asks for whether the terminal is connected. The tool gives *ready or not* and the message the till already shows (for example *Reader offline - no internet*), and never a terminal id, card attempt, amount or reference. Both tools' fields are `shop` data in the gate, so the owner's *Shop data* toggle can still switch them off. **(5) There is no printer to report.** 3.2 tool 15 mentions the printer, but the app has no printer connection (receipts go by QR code and email), so the tool says that in its note and the receipt page being set up is reported instead. **(6) Errors are scrubbed twice.** Each message is cut to one line of 160 characters with web addresses replaced by [address], then the gate masks emails, phone numbers, card numbers and keys as for every other tool. Notice bodies are never read, and refund and pass notices are left out because they name customers and staff. **(7) Both are snapshots,** taken when the question is asked, like the time and the screen context, so a tool cannot read or write the app. On practice data the snapshot is empty and the tools say they could not read the till (a second lock behind the practice mode block). The prompt now says fifteen tools for a cashier and sixteen for a manager or an owner. Patch 10 finishes the tool list; what is left in 3.10 is patch 8 (cash drawer, calculators and current cart) and patch 9 (practice mode coach). Next: patch 8, or patch 9.
 
